// work on this machine at the same time (several stories testing at once make every run slow and
// timing-sensitive tests fail).
//   test-slot <slots-dir> <command> [args…]
// The command's output and exit code pass through unchanged. A slot is a folder <slots-dir>/slot-N
// with the pid of its holder; the slot of a process that is gone is taken over. If no slot comes
// free in time, the command runs anyway — waiting must never stop a story. The command runs at a lower priority
// (nice), so the server, the pages and the agents stay responsive while tests work; it gets FACTORY_IN_TEST_SLOT=1,
// so the test gate of agent steps (tools/agent-bin) does not ask for a second slot inside this one.
